metal2vulkan runtime: host-visible memory that is not coherent, flushed and invalidated by the runtime (Scion)

Upstream:  metal2vulkan, https://github.com/steelbrain/metal2vulkan, at 720ef1ce9ae2a2068999a8675717418b9416283e, after
           AdrenoMetal's 16 patches to it (UniXNU/AdrenoMetal bridge/patches/, at ce5e19e33e05); tools/metal/mk-metal2vulkan.sh
           applies them in that order, then this.
Licence:   GPL-2.0-or-later OR LGPL-3.0-or-later, metal2vulkan's (its LICENSE); this patch is a change to it and under the same
           terms. Nothing of it is in Scion's MIT or APSL files.
Author:    the HakiOS authors (Scion), 29 October 2026.

Why. The runtime places Metal's Shared, Managed and WriteCombined memory, and its own host-visible buffers, only in
HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT types, and never flushes or invalidates. gfxstream's guest driver for Scion lists no such type
(it keeps a copy of each mapping in the guest), so the device was refused at its first allocation (OutOfMemory(Device)).

What. src/host_sync.rs says it in full:
- memory.rs: with no coherent host-visible type among those allowed, the host-visible ones; such placements take whole
  nonCoherentAtomSize atoms, so a flush of one carries none of a neighbour's bytes. Entry-point priming takes any
  host-visible type (it writes nothing through its mapping).
- command_buffer/submit.rs: before each batch, the command buffer's upload arena as written so far; at its first batch every
  program buffer its commands use, whole. The keys its tracked uses write are kept.
- command_buffer/mod.rs (complete): before its status and status words are read, the upload arena, and the program buffers
  its tracked uses write and those it uses untracked, whole; a buffer the GPU only reads is not invalidated.
- the runtime's own buffers written once by the host (zeros of a new buffer, a buffer made with bytes, texture staging and
  staged texels, fill and pattern bytes, a resident set's table, a tile map, block-decode shapes, a rate map's
  parameters): flushed after the write; what a host step reads of the GPU's writes, and getBytes staging: invalidated
  before the read.
- METAL2VULKAN_HOST_SYNC=always takes the same steps on coherent host-visible memory too.
Not covered: an indirect command buffer's records and a visible function table's words (written through pointers the
host keeps).

Checked: on lavapipe made non-coherent the way gfxstream's driver is (tools/metal/bridge/incoherent.rs,
HAKIOS_VK_INCOHERENT=1: every mapping a copy, bytes moved only by an explicit flush or invalidate, host image copy hidden),
tools/metal/m2v_test.c (the bridge's self-test, three kernels, a triangle) and tools/metal/metalvk-plugin-test.sh (the
Metal API: compute, render, blit, an IOSurface texture, replaceRegion and getBytes of a Shared texture) give every number
right with nothing between the runtime and the driver, where without this patch the device is refused. 1.0 MB flushed and
55 KB invalidated for all of m2v_test. On lavapipe and MoltenVK as they are (coherent), every check passes as before.

